WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.500 --> 00:00:05.020
Somewhere in a shared drive,
a contract is set to renew itself.

2
00:00:05.080 --> 00:00:10.040
The approval request bounces
from inbox to inbox, then sinks.

3
00:00:10.100 --> 00:00:14.500
The notice deadline passes.
Another year, locked in.

4
00:00:14.560 --> 00:00:20.080
And a telecom bill, $910 over
contract, gets paid anyway.

5
00:00:20.140 --> 00:00:22.890
Most companies don't
lose money on bad deals.

6
00:00:22.940 --> 00:00:26.180
They lose it on deals nobody was watching.

7
00:00:28.440 --> 00:00:33.253
Connexcy. Every contract.
Every invoice. Connected.

8
00:00:33.813 --> 00:00:37.373
Same renewal. This time,
Connexcy is watching.

9
00:00:37.533 --> 00:00:42.683
Send us what you have: drag in PDFs,
forward emails, or share a folder.

10
00:00:42.733 --> 00:00:46.493
Everything lands in one
secure, searchable place.

11
00:00:46.653 --> 00:00:50.643
Connexcy pulls out the key terms,
like dates, notice periods,

12
00:00:50.693 --> 00:00:55.613
auto-renewal clauses, pricing and owners,
and a person checks every one.

13
00:00:55.773 --> 00:00:59.163
It tracks the date that matters,
usually the notice deadline,

14
00:00:59.213 --> 00:01:04.333
not just the end date, and reminds
your team at 90, 60 and 30 days.

15
00:01:04.403 --> 00:01:06.913
Or set any schedule a contract needs,

16
00:01:06.963 --> 00:01:10.403
even a year ahead,
so there's time to shop around.

17
00:01:10.563 --> 00:01:13.393
Then it sends the renewal
to the people who decide,

18
00:01:13.443 --> 00:01:18.003
with a plain-English summary:
terms, cost and deadline.

19
00:01:18.213 --> 00:01:23.603
They can look back, too. Open any past
contract or invoice to see who approved it,

20
00:01:23.653 --> 00:01:29.043
everyone involved, and their notes on why
it was approved and why that vendor won.

21
00:01:29.093 --> 00:01:33.573
Maybe there's a reason you can't switch.
Or maybe it's time to look elsewhere.

22
00:01:33.833 --> 00:01:35.503
Before anyone signs off,

23
00:01:35.553 --> 00:01:39.463
Connexcy compares your contract with
other vendors for the same service,

24
00:01:39.513 --> 00:01:41.433
and shows you the price difference.

25
00:01:41.513 --> 00:01:46.393
Then you decide: renew, or switch
to the same outcome for less.

26
00:01:46.563 --> 00:01:49.633
And with our partner,
Global Bandwidth Technologies,

27
00:01:49.683 --> 00:01:55.113
a GBTech.ai expert can review your contract
and help you negotiate better terms,

28
00:01:55.163 --> 00:01:58.403
before you sign the
renewal or it auto-renews.

29
00:01:58.563 --> 00:02:00.883
Who decides depends on the amount.

30
00:02:00.963 --> 00:02:04.723
Small renewals go to one person.
Big ones go up the chain.

31
00:02:04.883 --> 00:02:09.363
Everyone sees who approved, who's
reviewing now, and who's up next.

32
00:02:09.443 --> 00:02:14.643
Sam signs off Tuesday. Waiting on Alex?
One click sends a friendly nudge.

33
00:02:15.503 --> 00:02:19.933
And that telecom bill? Every invoice is
matched to its contract, so anything

34
00:02:19.983 --> 00:02:24.863
that doesn't match, like an unapproved
rate increase, is flagged before you pay.

35
00:02:25.023 --> 00:02:31.583
Every contract, every deadline, every
invoice, all in one place, with time to act.

36
00:02:31.843 --> 00:02:35.043
Stop paying for renewals
you didn't choose.

37
00:02:35.303 --> 00:02:39.933
Connexcy is in beta now. Join the beta,
and our team will help you get set up.

38
00:02:39.983 --> 00:02:43.023
Or book a demo, at connexcy.com.
